WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.390
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.360
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.040
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.410
Mizuki-san's new unit, Tristar.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.190
The final member will be one of us.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.940
After one of us is chosen,

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.340
we might not see them again for the next few years.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.920
What I looked for in this audition

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.570
was the ability to shine as an idol even when alone.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.580
No matter who stands beside me, or whom I'm paired with,

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.090
even if that happens to be Tristar,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.180
Shibuki Ran will not change.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.850
I believe that, by bringing together those who have both a high level of professionalism

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.350
and the strength to shine alone, 
Tristar will become a top idol unit.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.440
The final member of Tristar will be...

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.450
Shibuki Ran!

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.960
You know, that pancake was really delicious.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.090
Ran...

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:10.460
Come on now, you're not acting like the Shibuki Ran I know.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.430
I-I can't help it...

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.970
It's the second time...

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.460
That I've had to leave my friends...

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.430
Ran.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.100
The runway is a road you walk down, 
carrying the feelings of lots of people.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.340
You're the one who taught me that.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.680
Take on Ichigo's, my, and everyone else's feelings {might have been wrong in the last episode}

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.270
and take off, Ran!

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.380
Smile, Ran!

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.560
<i>I've never felt like this before.</i>

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:59.000
<i>Everyone is waiting to see Tristar's debut.</i>

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.550
<i>Each and every one of my fans...</i>

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.020
<i>Mizuki-san...</i>

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.520
<i>I definitely won't let you down!</i>

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.270
Please prep Shibuki-san.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.560
It's almost time.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.030
Here we go.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.030
<i>Today, I am reborn.</i>

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.750
News about Ran is all over the place!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.660
I can't even begin to record it all...

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.340
She's on this channel too!

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:26.080
Record it for me! I'll put everything together later.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.760
The super-popular idol, Kanzaki Mizuki's new unit,

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.620
Tristar, had its debut event yesterday.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.050
Tristar was given its name because each one of us has the strength to shine alone.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.360
I'll show you a brilliance you've never seen before.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.380
And that's all for today's Tristar updates.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.180
Ran's so cool!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.640
I can't get enough of this!

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.030
"I'll show you a brilliance you've never seen before!"

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.480
Three points.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.830
Out of how many?

00:04:58.830 --> 00:04:59.930
One hundred.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.510
Just kidding.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:06.020
Come on, let's prepare Ran's gift bag.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.410
Sure.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:08.910
Letter, check.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.910
Same here. Masks and cough drops, both check.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.410
Seaweed, check!

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.590
Seaweed?!

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:18.420
It's a special kind that we use in our bento back at home.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:22.860
I'm sure Ran will get energized after crunching down on these.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.310
Crunchy crunchy crunchy. {I can't help but feel there's a better way to do periperiperiperi}

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.930
I can't see Ran eating it like that in a million years.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.930
You fink so?

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.760
Let's hurry over.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.380
Considering how busy Tristar will be, she might be getting ready to leave already.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.310
Sure.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:43.940
Huh?

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.950
I wonder what's going on?

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.830
Hoshimiya, Kiriya.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.640
Headmistress Orihime... what is this?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.820
Shibuki won't be returning to this dorm.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.330
Tristar's schedule is packed from dawn until dusk.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:15.350
They'll be even busier than Mizuki was during her solo career.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.980
Shibuki won't have any time to return here in the evening.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.610
Then where will she live?

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.610
Most likely, she'll spend her nights in hotels near her workplaces.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.560
It's a common occurrence among popular idols.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.370
I didn't expect her to be <i>this</i> busy...

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.910
She should be in the middle of a photo shoot right about now.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.920
Okay!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.140
Tristar, let's move out.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.920
Thank you for coming out here so early in the morning.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:59.090
Thanks a bunch!

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.190
Thank you very much.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.130
Shibuki, you're in the back.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:12.910
Okay.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.520
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>There are so many staff members on the bus.</i>

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.390
Good work with the photo shoot.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.420
Same to you.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.260
The day is young.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.660
We'll be recording a promotional video during the ride.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:42.190
After that, we're collecting data for two magazine articles.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.640
<i>Even on the bus, we don't get a break...</i>

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.110
Thank you for allowing us to work with you.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.130
Let's make a great video.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.690
Thank you very much.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.200
We don't have much time, so let's begin.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.580
Of course.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.200
Let's do this!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.630
Here we go.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.530
Three...

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:03.520
Good evening, viewers of "I RANK TV".

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.460
We're Tristar!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.390
Alright then, time for lunch.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:20.590
It's Raichi! It's Raichi!

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:19.810
Oh, Raichi.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:24.370
He aimed for the exact moment our lunch break started.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.630
I taught him well.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.610
Raichi, what's up?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.230
Onee-chaaan!

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.740
Isn't Ran-san amazing? Isn't she?

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.240
There's been so much news about Tristar today that I can't even begin to record it all.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:40.390
It's the same for me.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.750
Good afternoon, Aoi-neesan.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.340
Hey there.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.130
So, we have a favor to ask...

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.330
If you see Ran-san, please tell her we wish her luck!

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.010
You can do it!

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:54.810
Sure.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:59.170
But you know, even we can't really find the time to see her.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.050
Huh, really?

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:03.140
Tristar's really busy.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.610
I see...

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.080
But we'll make sure to tell her the next time we see her.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.970
We'll text her later.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.300
Thank you.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.700
You're so lucky, Raichi.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.780
Kiriya Aoi's the best.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.590
Did Onee-chan look kind of lonely?

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.470
I hope our gift basket gets to Ran soon.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.290
I'm sure it will.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:30.670
I'll tell some of the staff to hand it over for you.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.300
It'll get to her before long.

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.410
Let's send messages to Ran.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:38.300
That way we can be sure she sees it now.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.200
It's almost time for the show.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.560
Okay.

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:50.950
Tristar is here.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:53.070
Shibuki.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.070
Thank you.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.950
Girls, we'll be making an important announcement during the show.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.870
We were just notified of this.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.430
Yes!

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.330
I've always wanted to do something like this.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.670
It certainly is something 
Headmistress Orihime would do.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:17.680
We're about to start.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:20.700
And now for today's special corner.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.680
We've got an important announcement from Tristar!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:24.300
I wonder what it is!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.680
I can't wait to find out!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:31.440
Tristar will be holding a stadium live concert in commemoration of our founding. {?}

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.060
It's happening!

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.190
I've gotta go!

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.940
The location is at Big Stadium.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:39.750
And as for when it will be held...

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:40.950
It's tomorrow!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.210
Tomorrow?!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:47.120
I'm sure that there are those of you who won't be able to attend this surprise concert,

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.390
Does that mean tomorrow?

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.660
Like tomorrow next year?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.120
It means in one day.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.100
so we'll be streaming it live online.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.980
I've got an audition so I can't go!

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.030
I've got recording too...

00:10:56.210 --> 00:11:01.350
Befitting our name, each of Tristar's members will display their individual radiances

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.390
and bring you a Special Appeal unique to us.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:08.730
Yes! We'll be waiting for you at Big Stadium.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.980
Let's all have a lot of fun tomorrow.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.850
But why would they announce it only one day in advance?

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:18.410
Announcing unexpected concerts to gather widespread attention

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.400
is one of the basics of increasing sales.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:24.490
Haven't you heard of guerrilla lives before? {concert?}

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:26.940
Gorilla?

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:28.210
Not <i>that</i> kind.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.920
Guess we'll have to rely on these.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.660
Yeah, I won't miss it.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.730
Ran really is amazing.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:40.510
Didn't you notice? Even though she had no time to prepare,

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.380
she had a perfectly natural smile.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.510
She did!

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.440
Without any warning, huh.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.610
I can't help but be at least a bit surprised.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.680
Yeah, and she even reserved such a large stadium.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:57.330
This is an amazing chance for us, so let's make the most of it.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.530
You bet!

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.030
I will.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.030
I rented a space you can use for the night.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.320
Use it to train for tomorrow's concert.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.730
Thank you for everything.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.160
I love training! You always get out what you put in.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:12.960
Right.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:16.540
Welcome, honeys!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.620
Johnny-sensei!

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:26.300
I asked Johnny-sensei to do the choreography for Tristar, just like he always did for me.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.800
I'll be counting on you again.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.700
Please train us well.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:32.990
Now that you've got me here there'll be no problems.

00:12:32.990 --> 00:12:36.370
...or so I'd like to say, but we don't have much time.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.820
Let's focus on getting down the dance and getting out your Special Appeal.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:40.900
Okay!

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.380
<i>No!</i>

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:06.890
<i>Wow...</i>

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.050
<i>Mizuki-san and Kaede...</i>

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:12.620
<i>They've already memorized everything in such a short time...</i>

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.790
<i>If I can't catch up to them by tomorrow,</i>

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.600
<i>we won't be able to use Tristar's Special Appeal!</i>

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:23.740
<i>I can't...</i>

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.880
<i>I won't allow myself to hold them back!</i>

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:43.210
Let's wrap this up. Well done 
mastering everything, honeys.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.270
Thank you.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.410
We somehow made it in time.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.330
See you tomorrow.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.120
I know you'll be able to put on the best performance.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:55.630
Sleep well tonight.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.480
Thank you for the lesson.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.270
Let's all do our best tomorrow.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.280
Yes! Good night!

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.260
Sleep well.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.820
G-Good night.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.050
You should get some rest too, Ran.

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.340
R-Right.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.380
Good work today, and good night.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:25.520
I'm still nowhere near good enough yet!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.260
I knew I could count on those girls to prevail somehow.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.270
"Somehow" is an apt assessment.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.270
It's really not fair to give them only a single day's warning. {you sure love your split infinitives, don't you}

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:42.320
It's exactly because we're doing a surprise concert that it'll be big news.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:45.280
It's just like you to think of details like that.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:48.640
Understand that no matter how brightly a star may shine,

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.390
it's meaningless if there is nobody to see her.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:55.690
An idol's true job is to work hard for that radiance.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:15:00.670
And showing the world that that star is there is <i>my</i> job.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.220
There are two more...

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:08.100
Two more at Starlight who deserve to be brought into the spotlight.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:16.050
<i>I can't let Mizuki-san and Kaede's expectations of me down.</i>

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.680
<i>I'll show them how bright I can shine!</i>

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.100
<i>Shibuki Ran, is this...</i>

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:40.430
<i>Is this all you've got?!</i>

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.470
Morning!

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.390
Morning...

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.490
Did you forget that Tristar's stadium live is today?

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.290
That's right!

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:01.230
Let's send her texts for good luck.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.730
Sure.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.740
We're about to begin.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:15.610
Got it!

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.010
I was told that every seat sold out.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:26.400
Let's shine...

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.920
So brightly that they'll never forget!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:30.760
Yes!

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:30.760
Okay!

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.860
Triangle shiny light!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.340
Aoi, wasn't Ran great?

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.120
She was!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.620
They were in sync from the first step.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:55.630
I hope our gift basket and texts got to her alright.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:56.620
Yeah.

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:02.560
That felt awesome, right Mizuki?

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:06.080
Yes, I think we were able to put on a very unique performance.

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:37.490
<i>I may have been able to get by today without causing them any trouble or messing up,</i>

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.920
<i>but I was right on the line.</i>

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:42.700
<i>I'm not good enough...</i>

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:44.640
<i>I'm not—!</i>

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.430
Shibuki, good work.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:51.890
Thank you.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.870
Here. A gift from Hoshimiya and Kiriya.

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:57.060
Thank you for bringing it.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.230
<i>Ran, you can do it!</i>

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.130
<i>Go for it, Ran!</i>

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:20.090
<i>I can do it, huh.</i>

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.550
<i>Ran, let's do our best together!</i>

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.860
Why seaweed?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.920
It went exactly as you planned.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:22:02.310
Yes, Tristar's stadium live gathered more attention than I could have ever hoped for.

00:22:02.310 --> 00:22:04.920
But this is only the beginning.

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.090
To ensure the continued success of Starlight Academy,

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:12.180
I will make one more unit.

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:14.310
Are you talking about...

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:57.660
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism.

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:01.340
There are countless stars shining in the night sky.

00:24:01.340 --> 00:24:04.300
Picking out the brightest star from among them all...

00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:06.630
And telling the world is our job.

00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:09.840
Stars shine <i>because</i> they are gazed upon.

00:24:10.870 --> 00:24:12.280
Ran really is amazing!

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:14.030
The two of us can't let up either.

00:24:14.030 --> 00:24:16.720
That's right, because it's your turn next.

